From ee88b6307fc9e9f1ea4c2b205e6c09375c975332 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 13:30:23 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Add static requirement pages for search engines

The site had one indexable URL with about 90 words on it. Generate a
static page per program from the planner's own requirement rules, so
searches such as "AUBG computer science major requirements" have a
page to land on.

- backend/program_pages.py builds frontend/seo/programs.json from
  build_requirement_slots; a test fails when the committed file is stale
- frontend build writes /majors, /minors, one page per program and
  /general-education, plus 404.html and a full sitemap.xml
- 7 programs whose parsed requirements contradict the catalog PDF are
  skipped and named on the index pages instead of published wrong
- vercel.json rewrites only /p/:token to the app, so unknown URLs
  return a real 404 instead of the homepage
- /?major=<name> and /?minor=<name> open the setup screen with that
  program selected; the welcome screen links to the new pages

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
