From 18e9e65b0c2ce30f1994f9642fb292df3be2e002 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 14:00:36 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Correct program requirements and prerequisites against
 the catalog

Checked every program and course row against the AY 2025-26 catalog
PDF. All corrections are data in policy_overrides.json with a source
note, except one counting fix in the engine.

Requirements:
- Political Science major: POS 2002 is required and the choice is
  POS 2013 or EUR 2013 (was: POS 2013 required, EUR 2013 or POS 2002);
  electives are 19 credit hours, not "3 courses"
- Political Science minor: POS 2002 plus two of the other core courses
  (ten credit hours), not three fixed courses plus a choice
- Mathematics minor: MAT 2012 required, MAT 2001 or MAT 2013
- Literature major: ENG 2010, ENG 3088 and four of six surveys, not
  all six
- Southeast European Studies minor: two of five history courses plus
  twelve elective credit hours, not six required courses
- Modern Languages major: MLL 1075 required and 36 credit hours in
  total, not 18 with no required course
- Computer Science minor: 18 credit hours; the three group courses
  were counted on top of the 15 elective credit hours (9 courses)
- Physics minor: the 12 elective credit hours are now tracked

Prerequisites: restored for 34 courses whose description rows the PDF
parser missed, e.g. COS 4060 needs COS 2021 and INF 4040 needs
INF 3035 and senior standing.

Tests that pinned the old behaviour now assert what the catalog says,
and a new test checks each program's required plus elective credits
against the catalog's printed total. The five corrected programs get
requirement pages; general education pages list the courses the
planner credits through Excel tags.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013cnoiXrS5Ys8M8uLC9JuL8
